   377	  `confirmed_at ≤ declared + δ`. All three are evaluated together. [SPEC R-4.41:985; SPEC R-5.19:1352; SPEC
   378	  V33-V36:1342-1346; A9:99]
   379	- A real proof carries several attestations hours apart and nothing in the proof names T (M3). [FT:20; DD:98]
   380	- `OPEN (step 8):` one sentence stating whether T is the `anchor_time` of the three conjuncts. The sources use both
   381	  words and never equate them (A9:138, 249-250 use T and `anchor_time`; SPEC R-3.44:689-692 defines `anchor_time`).
   382	- `OPEN (step 8):` what "verified" means for an attestation: it must reach a pinned header at depth k. The
   383	  pruned-proof vectors at both window boundaries (DD:99) need this to be exact.
