   206	| Field | Bytes | Fixed by |
   207	|---|---|---|
   208	| tag length | [0, 1) | position |
   209	| tag | [1, 1+n) | byte 0 |
   210	| canonicalization version | [1+n, 3+n) | n |
   211	| length L | [3+n, 7+n) | n |
   212	| payload | [7+n, 7+n+L) | n and L |
   213	| end of input | at exactly 7+n+L | n and L; otherwise `TRUNCATED` or `TRAILING` |
   214	
   215	No boundary depends on the contents of a later field. In particular, the payload's own JSON structure never
   216	decides where the frame ends; the length does, which is A1 P8's "a parser cannot disagree about where the payload
   217	ends". The fields are then checked in order: tag in T and equal to `t` (Lemma 4); version equal to `0x0001`;
   218	`L ≤ 2^24`; payload in `Pay(t)` (Lemma 3(b) plus the schema).
