   220	For the first identity: given `frame(t, p)`, the decoder reads `n = |t|`, the tag `t`, `0x0001` and `L = |p|`. It
   221	finds exactly `L` bytes left, and those bytes are `p`. Then Lemma 3(b) applies.
   222	
   223	For the second identity: if `b` is accepted, every field equals the corresponding field of
