   190	## 4. Issue order (issuer side, binding on the build)
   191	
   192	1. Fix the manifest and common metadata, including `declared_issue_time`.
   193	2. Build both frames.
   194	3. Sign each frame.
   195	4. Verify both signatures with the exact bytes to be committed.
   196	5. Freeze the signature bytes. Any re-framing happens before this point.
   197	6. Build `A_sig` and stamp its SHA-256. One stamp per receipt.
   198	7. Obtain and validate the confirmation and time evidence.
   199	8. Ship the complete receipt.
   200	
   201	[ENC §5.4:515-525; A9:278-281] That is eight steps in both sources. A retry that changes any committed byte needs a
   202	fresh stamp. The frame-only anchor is withdrawn, with no fallback. [A9:277; ENC §5.1:407-414]
   203	
   204	Issuer duties that are not verifier rules: an attempt whose T would exceed not-after is not shipped [A9:341-342]; the
   205	`gpg` signer refuses a frame whose `declared_issue_time` is more than ε from its clock [A9:327-330]; the issuer never
   206	re-authorizes a key [A9:260]; public publication of the commit stays an issuer duty [A9:413-418]; the issuer
   207	re-captures the DNSSEC snapshot before shipping if it fails the snapshot rule [DD:94].
