   286	### 6.1 DNS channel
   287	
   288	- Owner name is `_tessera-v1.<D>`. The verifier rebuilds it from the signed `issuer` and compares label by label,
   289	  ignoring ASCII case. Anything else is `DNS_OWNER`. [ENC §7:551-556] This is the owner-name check (G-21 / M2).
   290	- One TXT RRset, one RR, one character-string. The value grammar, the fifteen-step rejection order and the
   291	  exact-255-byte rule are in ENC §7. [ENC §7:557-612]
   292	- The record carries `kms`, `gpg`, `profile`, `issuance-not-before` and `issuance-not-after`, all mandatory, in a
   293	  fixed order. [ENC §7:569-579]
   294	- The DNSSEC chain is validated against the root rule (section 5) at the snapshot's own anchored time (section 7.3).
   295	  [A9:137; A9:285-287]
   296	
   297	### 6.2 Issuance window (C4 verifier rule)
   298	
   299	- The window `issuance-not-after − issuance-not-before` is at most 90 days. A record that violates it is rejected
   300	  (`DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH`). V1 has one window and no overlap. [A9:334-337; ENC §7:578-580]
   301	- A receipt is `INVALID / ISSUANCE_WINDOW` unless `issuance-not-before` ≤ declared issue time and T ≤
   302	  `issuance-not-after`. Both bounds are inclusive. T is compared as registered, with no margin. T is not compared
   303	  with not-before. [A9:338-340; ENC §7.1:636-643, 662-663]
   304	- The guarantee is in chain time. A UTC cutoff would need a backward-skew bound V1 does not establish. [A9:360-366;
   305	  ENC §7.1:661-671]
   306	- A published window cannot be shortened. [A9:343]
   307	- The window, its dates and the stop margin are operating facts, not profile rules. [A9:341-342; RB §2]
