    40	## 1. The accepted domain, exactly
    41	
    42	Let **V** be the set of JSON values in E§1.1:
    43	- `null`, `true` and `false`;
    44	- finite binary64 numbers other than −0;
    45	- strings of Unicode scalar values that contain no noncharacter, no code point unassigned in Unicode 16.0.0, and are
    46	  in NFC;
    47	- arrays;
    48	- objects with pairwise distinct names.
    49	
    50	Two values are **equal** when they are equal as mathematical structures:
    51	- numbers are equal as doubles;
    52	- strings are equal as scalar sequences;
    53	- arrays are equal as sequences;
    54	- objects are equal as finite maps from names to values. Member order is not part of an object.
    55	
    56	That is the sense in which injectivity is claimed. Two JSON *texts* that differ only in spelling denote one value,
    57	and E§1.2 says why that is intended.
