    96	  §3.2.2.3) is a decimal literal whose round-half-even nearest double is `d`. Decimal-to-double conversion is
    97	  correctly rounded (IEEE 754). The ECMAScript specification requires both. The implementations rely on them
    98	  through `rfc8785` (A) and through `repr` and `float` (B).
    99	- **(H) SHA-256 collision resistance.** This is used **only** in Theorem part (iv) and Lemma 9, for the
