+| G09 / open trust intervals | How are open KSK/repository signing periods represented and closed without retroactive exclusion? | `docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:307-323`, `:324-332`; `docs/V1-PROFILE.md:250-251` | **Depends on future pre-freeze convention / silent.** A9 expressly delegates the endpoint/update convention; no format or concrete rule here. KSK-2024 end is open. | Stop. A later commit stamp is eligible if open means unbounded; it is unperformable if no finite authenticated end is available. Closing a period can change eligibility unless the specified non-retroactive convention is supplied. Keep finalized endpoints immutable. | **yes** |
