+| G11 / signature validation policy | Beyond mathematical ECDSA, must hashed critical/unknown subpackets, creation time, expiry or issuer metadata affect acceptance? Does the manifest possession proof use the same serialization rule? | `formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md:324-337`, `:366-370`, `:444-468`, `:498-513`, `:654-658`, `:806-807`; `formal/p8/PROOF.md:105-110` | **Silent at verifier-policy layer.** Codec explicitly ignores subpacket contents; unhashed area has no meaning and key expiry is not relied on. P3 profile is outside P8. Hashed critical-content handling and possession serialization are not settled here. | Stop at math/policy verification; do not import a generic OpenPGP keyring policy. A mathematically verifying packet with an unknown critical hashed subpacket can pass pure ECDSA verification and fail a standards-oriented OpenPGP validator. Do not add revocation or current-time expiry checks. | **yes** |
